 b(x)y\' + c(x)y = f(x), which of the following represents a Second-Order Linear Homogeneous ODE?','mcq','[\"y\'\' + xy\' + y^2 = 0\", \"x^2y\'\' + sin(x)y\' + 3y = 0\", \"y\'\' + y\'y = 0\", \"y\'\' + 2y\' + y = x\"]','1',NULL,1,5,'2025-10-10 04:22:14.285000','0a43196b3ca94ea9b55f955d79081eb5'),('500ce3092bdc462888a75c8e4729043a','The text mentions several real-world applications for Second-Order Linear Differential Equations. Which of the following is NOT listed as an example?','mcq','[\"Predicting the swing of a bridge.\", \"Modeling the vibration of a guitar string.\", \"Designing circuits with specific frequencies.\", \"Calculating the trajectory of a projectile in a vacuum.\"]','3',NULL,1,4,'2025-10-10 04:49:32.228000','5fad0c9e38ef4d738b63eeec385fe100'),('5024c5f3fd024b5fa50cbd3fc9ab6a6c','What will `fibonacci(4)` return in the provided code example?','mcq','[\"2\", \"3\", \"4\", \"5\"]','1',NULL,1,5,'2025-09-23 10:13:33.609000','470e5f71014944ff848a5fc0afc92718'),('5024c9fe6ecb4778ba048a08d3f684b0','Which order type is designed to limit potential losses by selling an asset if the price drops to a certain point?','mcq','[\"Limit Order\", \"Market Order\", \"Stop-Loss Order\", \"Buy Order\"]','2',NULL,1,4,'2025-09-22 12:49:20.740000','5ef9526ec04b41eb97dc2639b1f6c145'),('506d65d295ea4d2f9b014b9c5d3dd4fc','What does it mean if a system of linear equations has no solution?','mcq','[\"The lines representing the equations are parallel.\", \"The lines representing the equations are the same.\", \"The lines representing the equations intersect at one point.\", \"The lines representing the equations are perpendicular.\"]','0',NULL,1,3,'2025-09-22 13:04:13.052000','420eb210237e4090abb9641053783830'),('5084c921ffbe4de9a5df303410e0468a','If you know the adjacent side and the angle, which trigonometric function would you use to find the opposite side?','mcq','[\"Cosine\", \"Sine\", \"Tangent\", \"Cosecant\"]','2',NULL,1,4,'2025-09-25 12:59:54.626000','d74592981391499e8b8