uce the computational cost of model training.\", \"To ensure the data is of high quality and contains the most relevant information, significantly impacting the model\'s ability to learn and make accurate predictions.\", \"To solely visualize data patterns without training a model.\", \"To automate the entire machine learning pipeline without human intervention.\"]','1',NULL,1,4,'2025-10-08 10:48:51.989000','3921f356c51641d498226e1711b0788c'),('54a8f76a78434eb9b179f475116aa3f7','What kind of real-world paths or shapes are often described by quadratic equations?','mcq','[\"Straight lines\", \"Zig-zag patterns\", \"\\\"U-turn\\\" curves or arcs\", \"Perfect circles\"]','2',NULL,1,1,'2025-10-07 06:25:58.989000','b9a164d3c5b7434e96636a3d473e2a4b'),('54d858ba45ee4842a82e352c610d0499','If you know the angle of elevation and the distance from an object, which trigonometric function would you use to find the height of the object?','mcq','[\"Cosine\", \"Sine\", \"Tangent\", \"None of the above\"]','2',NULL,1,3,'2025-09-25 17:50:02.048000','1204664ce0cf410fa019d5ce76bdd3fe'),('5507419d07a3418fbdf29bd991f66892','In the tree example, why was the tangent function used to calculate the height of the tree?','mcq','[\"Because the angle of elevation and the hypotenuse were known.\", \"Because the angle of elevation and the adjacent side were known.\", \"Because the height of the tree and the adjacent side were known.\", \"Because the height of the tree and the hypotenuse were known.\"]','1',NULL,1,4,'2025-09-25 13:40:19.988000','d65f0f8a25284e4aa6d45c3e9be97f09'),('5507da2539cf478aacc4df9fd78ae89a','For which type of problems is a recursive solution often considered more intuitive and readable than an iterative one, according to the text?','mcq','[\"Problems requiring extensive database queries.\", \"Problems that have a naturally recursive structure.\", \"Problems best solved with simple linear iteration.\", \"Problems that involve only basic arithmetic operations.\"]','1',NULL,1,5