, what does the term \"Ordinary\" signify?','mcq','[\"The equation is simple to solve.\", \"The function depends on only one independent variable.\", \"The equation describes common, everyday phenomena.\", \"The highest derivative is of the first order.\"]','1',NULL,1,1,'2025-10-10 04:12:32.246000','4599b3db47cf48ea86267db773236641'),('5748a48e3c0646d69a45c68c4aa9c73b','Let V be a vector space. Which of the following is NOT necessarily a subspace of V?','mcq','[\"{0}, the set containing only the zero vector.\", \"V itself.\", \"The set of all vectors in V multiplied by a fixed scalar k.\", \"The union of two subspaces of V.\"]','3',NULL,1,2,'2025-09-22 13:04:13.101000','d0c51f8abe2d430ea608e3febc1f251e'),('575b04e2fb4f43a298d8ea8f78853e7e','What is the main role of the Sun in our solar system, as described in the text?','mcq','[\"To create new planets and moons.\", \"To act as a giant, never-ending nuclear furnace providing light and heat.\", \"To serve as a solid surface for celestial objects to land on.\", \"To repel objects away from the center of the solar system.\"]','1',NULL,1,3,'2025-10-07 06:34:38.388000','bdb724c12e6f4e8eba35f6ab62281883'),('57701affe79d420d8b9c843bf983cd32','In C++, what happens when you try to access an array element outside of its defined bounds?','mcq','[\"The compiler automatically resizes the array.\", \"The program throws a specific \\\"OutOfBounds\\\" exception.\", \"It leads to undefined behavior or program crashes.\", \"The value at index 0 is returned.\"]','2',NULL,1,4,'2025-09-22 13:35:25.021000','cae5db6c04d64f4690af967d183635e4'),('57c428c221d44ce591b04e9977250780','In the context of differential equations, what is the key characteristic that defines an Ordinary Differential Equation (ODE)?','mcq','[\"It involves functions of multiple independent variables.\", \"It relates an unknown function to its partial derivatives.\", \"It involves functions of a single independent variable and their ordinary derivatives.\", \"It always has a constant solution.\"]','2',NULL,1,2,'2025-10-10 04:11:14.260000','aae4ce9acb1c4afeba814726a675d550'),('57c447687495406ca2097c9e4b28f009','Which of the following is a valid solution to the differential equation dy/dx = 2x?','mcq','[\"y = x²\", \"y = x² + 5\", \"y = 2x\", \"y = x\"]','1',NULL,1,2,'2025-09-25 13:06:14.222000','eff0705446ba4e4cb991a2430a13dd0c'),('57c486d94ccd470e9d2a33f98cee35a9','How is the 90-degree angle in a right triangle typically marked?','mcq','[\"With a circle\", \"With an arrow\", \"With a small square\", \"With a star\"]','2',NULL,1,3,'2025-10-07 05:29:58.413000','f6e190ababf54d3e8a4bc877ef9c5f1f'),('5845484369a740c0b8a9626ceb83a301','What does it mean if a system of linear equations has infinitely many solutions?','mcq','[\"The lines representing the equations are parallel.\", \"The lines representing the equations are the same.\", \"The lines representing the equations intersect at one point.\", \"The lines representing the equations are perpendicular.\"]','1',NULL,1,5,'2025-09-22 13:04:13.060000','420eb210237e4090abb9641053783830'),('584f626494d541ffbb96a4103ae080d0','Which of the following best describes an angle?','mcq','[\"A single line extending infinitely in one direction.\", \"A point where two lines intersect.\", \"Formed by two rays that share a common endpoint.\", \"A closed two-dimensional shape with three sides.\"]','2',NULL,1,3,'2025-10-08 11:47:28.902000','491ae6426cb347c5b61af6bdbc1e92b2'),('588fa83d0dbf4ff0bbf30a85fbc2f74d','How does Machine Learning (ML) relate to Artificial Intelligence (AI) based on the provided content?','mcq','[\"AI is a subset of ML.\", \"ML is a powerful subset of AI.\", \"AI and ML are two entirely separate and unrelated fields.\", \"ML is an older technology that AI has replaced.\"]','1',NULL,1,3,'2025-10-08 11:39:09.756000','63a698377af14babb08a8ccff74bd333'),('58ec791a461a48d683d6e7484edacfc3','Which of the following best describes a \"string\" in programming?','mcq','[\"A single numerical value.\", \"A sequence of characters.\", \"A collection of true/false values.\", \"A memory address.\"]','1',NULL,1,1,'2025-10-08 03:59:29.921000','c454e6e34f914a0abbc824a90665c214'),('59931d71734e42f88ead52a2fcc927f7','What is the role of a \"visited\" set in a Breadth-First Search (BFS) algorithm?','mcq','[\"To store the nodes yet to be explored.\", \"To keep track of the nodes already explored, preventing cycles.\", \"To store the path from the start node to the current node.\", \"To prioritize nodes for exploration based on their distance from the start node.\"]','1',NULL,1,4,'2025-09-23 10:03:17.434000','e1de9d36952e422885e3f8cd84f5e660'),('59f848b07f6c44d1888e386ecd9341e9','Which of the following is a differential equation?','mcq','[\"$y = x^2 + 2x + 1$\", \"$dy/dx = 2x$\", \"$∫x dx = x^2/2 + C$\", \"$f(x) = sin(x)$\"]','1',NULL,1,2,'2025-09-25 13:46:54.504000','85f6214e0955429e8a31982637302795'),('5a14ddc1bd2f44bb9bd712a20bc57e8d','What is the value of sin^2(45°) + cos^2(45°)?','mcq','[\"0\", \"0.5\", \"1\", \"2\"]','2',NULL,1,4,'2025-09-25 17:50:02.050000','1204664ce0cf410fa019d5ce76bdd3fe'),('5a6b1e5cedd640798415bf75bdd794e8','Which term in the damped oscillation equation `m * (d²x/dt²) + c * (dx/dt) + kx = 0` represents the damping force?','mcq','[\"m * (d²x/dt²)\", \"c * (dx/dt)\", \"kx\", \"0\"]','1',NULL,1,5,'2025-09-25 13:06:14.238000','eff0705446ba4e4cb991a2430a13dd0c'),('5a8b8c9bc63445de96d81daa71f140ef','What does a derivative represent in the context of a function?','mcq','[\"The average rate of change of the function.\", \"The instantaneous rate of change of the function.\", \"The maximum value of the function.\", \"The minimum value of the function.\"]','1',NULL,1,1,'2025-09-25 12:43:33.199000','cc36eeb508fb4a23ab995c460d644a32'),('5b22043203424bb7b8b923e189404a70','How do React Hooks, specifically `useState` and `useEffect`, empower functional components compared to their pre-Hooks state?','mcq','[\"They allow functional components to use `this` 