parable differential equation?','mcq','[\"Integration of both sides.\", \"Solving for y.\", \"Separation of variables.\", \"Plotting the slope field.\"]','2',NULL,1,4,'2025-09-25 17:45:26.432000','e49b8b7355d7429ca5f59288cd17478a'),('5f8aeb554db144c09a93b8a0df65dc39','What is the general solution to the differential equation $dy/dx = 2x$?','mcq','[\"$y = x^2$\", \"$y = 2x + C$\", \"$y = x^2 + C$\", \"$y = x^3/3 + C$\"]','2',NULL,1,3,'2025-09-25 13:46:54.506000','85f6214e0955429e8a31982637302795'),('5f95a2ce3c064ca397c012b7d3a8ebd9','In the separation of variables technique, what is the crucial first step?','mcq','[\"Integrating both sides of the equation.\", \"Rewriting the equation to isolate the variables on different sides.\", \"Solving for the dependent variable.\", \"Determining the constant of integration.\"]','1',NULL,1,3,'2025-09-25 17:24:08.288000','f88ff020fc0841afb824fcd12e89ec32'),('60e0bdaa32e84afa9ca9a546257dd6af','In a right triangle, the \"Adjacent Side\" is defined as the side next to the specific acute angle of focus. What other condition must it meet?','mcq','[\"It must be the longest side.\", \"It must be opposite the 90-degree angle.\", \"It must *not* be the hypotenuse.\", \"It must be shorter than the opposite side.\"]','2',NULL,1,5,'2025-10-08 17:01:49.741000','a7fb522bd62546d9b06810a8c5579b76'),('61298b11c5ea48e8b3f10fec5181bf55','Which of the following is a separable differential equation?','mcq','[\"dy/dx = x + y\", \"dy/dx = x * y^2\", \"dy/dx = x/y + y/x\", \"dy/dx = sin(x*y)\"]','1',NULL,1,5,'2025-09-25 17:45:26.433000','e49b8b7355d7429ca5f59288cd17478a'),('61310250091e4242ae757b8b5cd76305','When identifying the \"opposite\" and \"adjacent\" sides in a right triangle, what is crucial to remember?','mcq','[\"They always stay the same regardless of the angle.\", \"They only change if the triangle is rotated.\", \"They change depending on which acute angle you are focusing on.\", \"They are only relevant for the hypotenuse.\"]','2',NULL,1,