.\"]','1',NULL,1,4,'2025-09-22 14:13:35.460000','1249b9ae5a314fa18d98c4ffb3cee778'),('81b41143dc1d4f318ce132ab5c1aeaa6','What does the term \"homogeneous\" mean in the context of second-order linear differential equations?','mcq','[\"The coefficients a(x), b(x), and c(x) are constant.\", \"The forcing function f(x) is equal to zero.\", \"The equation has only one solution.\", \"The equation can be solved using separation of variables.\"]','1',NULL,1,3,'2025-09-25 17:24:08.330000','8cfc3c86b4e74d76961da48ee126de45'),('81d69fdc967d4c4daf43d0cd62771d66','What does it mean for strings to be immutable in languages like Java and Python?','mcq','[\"Strings can be modified directly after creation.\", \"String modifications create new string objects.\", \"Strings cannot be used for text manipulation.\", \"Strings have a fixed maximum length.\"]','1',NULL,1,4,'2025-09-22 15:12:29.114000','fdea55712a3b4cad965bef691bfac247'),('81db7ebce8894aa1a06a227c83841948','Which of the following is a valid example of a differential equation?','mcq','[\"$y = x^2 + 2x + 1$\", \"$dy/dx = y$\", \"$∫ x dx = x^2/2 + C$\", \"$x + y = 5$\"]','1',NULL,1,2,'2025-09-25 08:21:47.230000','f58716d1fde34d33b2303a0b2260771e'),('82494a310e114dd389dda7ddd0f689a5','The Laplace Transform primarily converts differential equations into what type of equations?','mcq','[\"Integral equations\", \"Algebraic equations\", \"Trigonometric equations\", \"Partial differential equations\"]','1',NULL,1,2,'2025-10-10 04:22:14.375000','580ab48eb18e4e8baee457a0401cc668'),('82aa4712daf74268bb1a19ff90512a39','What is the primary purpose of Dynamic Programming?','mcq','[\"To perform complex mathematical calculations.\", \"To break down problems into smaller overlapping subproblems and store solutions to avoid redundant computations.\", \"To search large datasets efficiently.\", \"To represent relationships between entities using nodes and edges.\"]','1',NULL,1,2,'2025-09-23 10:03:17.430000','e1de9d36952e422885e3f8cd84f5e660'),(